  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-11> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-11--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-11--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch12-11: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.64" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.639"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.77"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Convergence is testable when morphology is mapped onto a phylogeny inferred from independent characters. Existing data can establish examples but likely cannot estimate how often it happened across all Foraminifera." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Map quantified shell forms onto independently inferred molecular and fossil phylogenies and count repeated origins of near-identical morphologies. Multiple distant lineages converging beyond uncertainty would support the claim; forms restricted to single clades would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Sparse molecular sampling and uncertain fossil placement.", "Identical form requires an explicit morphometric tolerance." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-11--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-11--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-11--gpt--dataset-3> .
